From efb286960a19a2dec6008486e511205cb2baf511 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:59:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] U28: Read the whole story in 2027

The Study Bible's story path (story.json, every chapter once in story order) cut into 365 days of about the same length by word count, each act starting on a day of its own, each day linking the context guide whose first key text it reads. Generated and committed by scripts/build-story-plan.mjs (client/public/bible/guides/whole-story-2027.json), with a --check drift and soundness gate in CI.

The page /study/bible/guides/whole-story-2027 (StudyBibleYear.tsx, lib/storyPlan.ts) opens on the day in the address, else the reader's place on this device, else today's day in 2027, else day 1; lists the day's chapters as doors into the Study Bible on the story path; marks a day read on the device; shows position, never a count behind; and offers a daily reminder (RemindMe gains an optional start date, so it can begin January 1). The year below by month renders only open months. My Library lists the plan by the reader's place.

Linked from the Study hub, the guides index, and the story page; registered in App.tsx (before the guide param route), the sitemap, the prerendered head with a crawlable list of the days, and llms.txt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JuCQ8kZ25i9zRwNgk6bh4e
